Using the dataset from run 3 of the LHC, the collaboration measured the differential decay rate for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ process relative to the squared decay rate of the $e^{+}e^{-}ightarrow\mu^{+}\mu^{-}$ reaction. To obtain this, they analyzed the joint decay chains of $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ and $D_s^{*-}ightarrow D_s^{-}\gamma$, as well as $ ar{B}_s^0ightarrow ar{D}_s^{*+}\mu^{-} ar{
u}_{\mu}$ and $D_s^{*+}ightarrow D_s^{+}\gamma$. The final differential decay rate with respect to $w$ (the scaled recoil velocity of the $D_s^{*}$) was derived by combining 2020 and 2019 data samples. The resulting function was then fitted to calculate the product of the normalisation factor and the form factor $f_1(M_{carrying}^{*})$ at specific recoil velocities.
